<title>SOUTH AFRICA: African &amp; Overseas year income flat.</title>
<headline>African &amp; Overseas year income flat.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		 62.7	  vs 65.3</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 23.75	 vs same</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   6.49	  vs 6.53</p>
<p>    Interest received     2.56	  vs 1.70</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   18.18	 vs 15.87</p>
<p>    Tax			 6.91	  vs 4.54</p>
<p>    Turnover		  215.38	vs 194.29</p>
<p>Full name: African &amp; Overseas Enterprises Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - African &amp; Overseas, whose principal operating division is Rex Trueform Clothing Co Ltd, said it had recommended a capitalisation share award in the form of &quot;N' ordinary shares. However, ordinary and &quot;N&quot; ordinary shareholders on the register at November 8 can elect instead to receive a cash dividend of 23.75 cents a share.</p>
<p>The firm said it would open four new Queenspark stores in 1996 and eight more in 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
